  extends ThermoSysPro.UsersGuide.Documentation.ThermoSysProPackageIcon;
  annotation(Documentation(info = "## Copyright © EDF 2002 - 2025

## ThermoSysPro Version 4.2

Machines  


Water/steam machines are very common since the invention of steam engines in the 18th century. Centrifugal pumps, compressors and generators are available as components here.  

For a better understanding of the underlying physics of the Stodola turbine, see Chap. 10 of :cite:`el19`.  
For a better understanding of the underlying physics of the centrifugal pumps, see Chap. 12 of :cite:`el19`.  



     

